  "turn d1 m3 s0": "## Stage now: 2 Understand
Do: react to the buyer's last answer, then ask one question that changes which products you recommend. You have 3 questions left before you must recommend. Answering the buyer's own questions does not use them.
Ask the questions needed for the quote first. A question that helps the pitch is asked once, without insisting. If the buyer skips it, move on and do not ask it again in the next messages. You may come back to it once, later, only when it fits what the buyer is talking about, woven into your reply: never as a quiz, and never holding up the next step. Drop it when the buyer shows a buying signal. Record each question you start with update_deal_state asked.
Moves on when: you know enough to recommend one set. If you already do, recommend now (stage 3) and ask nothing more.
Still missing for a quote: Business type.
Prices: not yet. State no price and no total. If the buyer asks the price, call update_deal_state with price_asked true, then answer with a number or range from search_catalog.
Paused: the buyer has an open objection ("price"). Settle it first: acknowledge, give the approved answer, check that it settled it. Record it as handled, then return to the stage.
